writeMd("miller-north-three-province-owner-synthesis-2026-09-06.md", `# Miller North three-province owner synthesis\n\n> Private owner-review artifact. No publication decision.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Built three deep, source-backed provincial cases: In Plain Sight, the Saskatoon coerced-sterilization cohort, and Alberta's Indigenous Primary Health Care Advisory Panel implementation chain.\n- Preserved the exact 24-recommendation B.C. ledger and added an eight-theme visual projection.\n- Resolved the PIDA numbering conflict in favour of canonical recommendation 11 and documented the current-page inconsistency.\n- Updated Saskatchewan's legal status: class certification was dismissed in 2025, without deciding individual merits.\n- Completed Red Deer-first Alberta selection and explicitly rejected weaker local cases rather than forcing a dossier.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe Farm can now explain three materially different accountability structures using one private, human-readable research projection. It also shows the recurring limit: public reporting often documents selected actions more clearly than it reports every recommendation or measures outcomes.\n\n## Strongest evidence\n\n- B.C.: original review, 24-month task-team report, current Action 3.07 reporting and Indigenous-led governance evaluation.\n- Saskatchewan: commissioned external review, SHA response/evaluation/current service page, parliamentary report and 2025 court-case digest.\n- Alberta: 22-recommendation panel report, The Way Forward, current grant/fund/advocate pages and Red Deer source screening.\n\n## Uncertainty / caution\n\n- Missing disaggregated reporting is not non-implementation.\n- Program creation is not provincewide operation or effectiveness.\n- The Saskatchewan certification result is procedural, and Bill S-228 is later context only.\n- Treaty geography is not a legal-right conclusion.\n- Public-role people are private contextual candidates, not a public people database.\n\n## Recommended next move\n\nRun one owner-approved, organization-specific status-ledger request per province, starting with B.C.'s 24 recommendations because that case has the strongest baseline and clearest reporting discrepancy.\n\n## Key metrics\n\n- Cases: 3\n- B.C. recommendations tracked: 24\n- Alberta candidates screened: ${abCandidates.length}\n- Bounded knowledge-gap follow-ups: 3 (answered: 1; partially answered: 2)\n- Public-role people recorded: ${people.length}\n- Evidence edges: ${validation.evidence_edges}\n- Source references: ${validation.sources}\n- Production mutations: 0\n- Publication mutations: 0\n- Migrations: 0\n\n## Operations\n\n- Web-search calls: ${operations.web_search_calls}\n- Source-inspection calls: ${operations.source_inspection_calls}\n- Registered authoritative source families used: ${operations.authoritative_source_families_used}\n- Tavily calls: 0\n- Local-model calls: 0\n- Cloud-model API calls: 0\n- Measurable external cost: $0\n`)

